    "content": [
      {
        "signature": "",
        "thinking": "I'm recognizing this as a Rawls veil-of-ignorance question where maximin applies. I need to match the two societies to the options, since Society B is better for everyone except those at the very bottom, with less safety net but more wealth at the top.\n\nI'm settling on answering with B, since behind the veil a risk-averse chooser would take the secure minimum, though one could argue B is more prosperous for most people. It's a value judgment, so I'll say so and keep the reasoning brief.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "**B**: Behind a veil of ignorance, I'd prioritize avoiding the worst outcome. Society B's better average comes with a harder life at the bottom, and I can't rule out landing there. A secure floor of housing, healthcare, and education protects against catastrophe, and the gap in prosperity is less important to me than that guarantee.",
        "type": "text"
      }
    ],
